      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Extremist recruitment rhetoric during that era heavily relied on framing an \"us vs. them\" binary, often positioning the in-group as virtuous and under existential threat. A key theme was the policing of \"traditional values,\" which they weaponized to equate social change with moral decay. They frequently utilized fear-based appeals, suggesting that racial or social minorities posed an immediate danger to the perceived purity and stability of white, working-class America. Analyzing these underlying thematic structures, rather than the language itself, should provide you with robust material for your linguistic coding.",
